# How to cite MyoDishAnalysis. GitHub shows this as "Cite this repository" (APA, BibTeX).
# After the first release: add the Zenodo concept DOI (identifiers).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "MyoDishAnalysis"
abstract: >-
  Analysis of MyoDish recordings (.mdd) in MATLAB and Python: parameters of every single contraction,
  reference beat, removal of the periodic rocker artifact, alignment of a parallel electrophysiological
  recording (LabChart) and action potential parameters. Command-line functions and an interactive GUI;
  the MATLAB and Python versions give the same results.
authors:
  - family-names: "Seidel"
    given-names: "Thomas"
    affiliation: "Institute of Cellular and Molecular Physiology, Friedrich-Alexander-Universität Erlangen-Nürnberg (FAU); InVitroSys GmbH"
    email: "thomas.seidel@fau.de"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3127-1693"
version: "1.0.0-beta.4"
date-released: "2026-10-10"
license: "GPL-3.0-or-later"
repository-code: "https://github.com/TS-IVS/MyoDishAnalysis"
# identifiers:
#   - type: doi
#     value: "10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX"
#     description: "Concept DOI (all versions)"
keywords:
  - myocardial slices
  - living myocardial slices
  - cardiac tissue culture
  - MyoDish
  - contractility
  - force measurement
  - action potential
  - MATLAB
  - Python
